<SolutionPage
  title="Environmental Health"
  parent="Mitigate"
  oneliner="Your environment is dictating your biology 24/7 whether you notice or not."
  slug="environment"
>
  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Light spectrum, air quality, water quality, EMF exposure, and contact with the earth —
    these aren't fringe concerns. They are high-leverage biological inputs because they change
    the dose-response of every other protocol you run. You can eat clean, train hard, sleep
    well, and still be systematically undermined by what's in your air, water, and light
    environment.
  </p>
  <p>
    Modern indoor environments are poorly matched to human biology. Artificial blue-spectrum
    light tells the brain it's noon all night. Tap water delivers endocrine-disrupting
    compounds with every glass. Indoor air carries volatile organic compounds, mold spores,
    and cooking particulates at levels that exceed outdoor air quality in most homes. Chronic
    EMF immersion from routers, phones, and smart meters is an uncontrolled experiment we are
    all enrolled in.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Mitigate pillar of 4M addresses environment as a modifiable exposure, not a fixed
    condition. Small, targeted interventions in your immediate environment produce compounding
    benefit across every other pillar.
  </p>

  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <p>These are the environmental inputs silently loading your biology every day.</p>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>LED bulbs emitting nothing but blue-spectrum light — active in the bedroom and living areas all night</li>
    <li>No morning sun exposure — the circadian signal that sets your master clock never fires</li>
    <li>Drinking unfiltered tap water — fluoride, chlorine, PFAS, microplastics, and chloramines delivered daily</li>
    <li>Indoor air full of VOCs, mold spores, and cooking particulates with no filtration</li>
    <li>Constant EMF immersion — router in the bedroom, phone in the pocket all day, sleeping next to chargers</li>
    <li>Feet never in contact with the earth — modern footwear and flooring eliminate grounding entirely</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-eliminate">Eliminate the Insulting Behavior</h2>
  <p>Prioritize the two highest-exposure areas in your environment first. Then work outward.</p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 1 — Swap Bedroom Bulbs</h3>
      <p>Replace LED overhead bulbs in bedroom and living areas with circadian-friendly warm-spectrum bulbs. Immediate biological impact on melatonin production.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 2 — HEPA + Carbon Air Filtration</h3>
      <p>A quality HEPA + activated carbon unit in the bedroom removes particulates, VOCs, and biological contaminants while you sleep. Highest ROI per dollar of any air intervention.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 3 — Filter Your Water</h3>
      <p>Under-sink reverse osmosis or whole-home strong-carbon filtration removes fluoride, PFAS, chlorine, and microplastics. Add a shower filter for skin and inhalation exposure.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 4 — Morning Sun on Your Eyes</h3>
      <p>5–10 minutes of direct sunlight — no glasses — within 30 minutes of waking. This single signal anchors your entire circadian rhythm for the day.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 5 — Ground Daily</h3>
      <p>Bare feet on grass, soil, or sand for 20+ minutes. If you can't, use a grounding mat indoors. Electrical contact with earth reduces inflammatory markers measurably.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

